Start Java learning java is high level object oriented programming language.

# Setup Notes
-> Download JDK (Temurin 25 lts(Long term Support))
-> Install Ide intellij
-> Plugins :- Atom Material Icon , Rainbow Bracket , Lombok Linting Tool
-> Link GitHub :- Search > Setting > Version Control > GitHub Search > Add Account > Link Done


# Pushing Code to GitHub
-> GItHUb OPen > Create Repo > Follow step
--> Terminal > git init (This will Initialise git in our project)
               git add . (. is use to add all the change we have done in our code.)
               git add "File name" (This will only push that particular file changes only)

               git status (It will show the status of all the file changes which should be tracked or untracked . Green for tracked and red for untracked)
               git commit -m "Message about the changes" (commit - This will push the code and -m is for message)
